# General Guidelines

- Write clean, self-documenting code. Favor readability over clever one-liners.
- Do not introduce new dependencies without explaining why they are strictly necessary.
- Follow strict typing: avoid `any`, untyped dictionaries, or implicit types where the language supports static typing.
- Always handle errors explicitly at network, file, and database boundaries; never silently catch and ignore exceptions.
- Keep functions small and focused on a single responsibility.